  "script": "Sneakers earned a write-up? My new manager loved rules more than results, so I followed every line after her business casual violation. Page fourteen said visible tattoos must be covered. Nobody told the warehouse crew; within a day, half looked recruited by a long sleeve cult. Page twenty two allowed personal calls only on the break room landline. At lunch, the whole floor queued for one beige phone like the last parking spot before a blizzard. Page thirty required safety vests at all times on the production floor\u2014which technically includes the bathroom. I wore mine there. By the third day, corporate called: productivity had dropped nineteen percent. By the end of the week, the handbook quietly changed. My sneakers stayed on my feet, unwritten up, for good. Which rule broke first: Page fourteen, Page twenty two, or Page thirty?",
